# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the agendi project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` using pnpm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` with the resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the body section of the root layout
- Positioned the Analytics component after existing components (TooltipProvider and Toaster) to ensure proper initialization

## Framework Details
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.3.6 (App Router)
- **Package Manager**: pnpm
- **Installation Method**: Followed Next.js App Router instructions from official Vercel documentation

## Implementation Approach
The implementation follows the recommended approach for Next.js App Router:
1. The Analytics component is imported from `@vercel/analytics/next`
2. It's added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
3. Placed inside the `<body>` tag for proper page tracking

## Verification
- ✅ No linting errors introduced in the modified file
- ✅ All existing tests passed (2,167 tests across 67 test files)
- ✅ Lock files properly updated
- ⚠️ Build verification skipped (requires MongoDB environment variables for existing app functionality)

## Next Steps
To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Verify tracking by checking for network requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` in the browser's Network tab

## Notes
- The existing project had a pre-existing linting error in `src/hooks/use-mobile.ts` (unrelated to this change)
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views once the app is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required - analytics will work out of the box after Vercel deployment
